s first record, in Unix milliseconds, and the other 74 bits that aren’t the version and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"variant are random, never derived from the device, the user or another identifier. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enricher keeps it in memory only, so a new tracker, as on the next launch, starts a new session","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a new identifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store keeps it beside each record of the session, as part of the record’s own bytes, and it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is deleted when the store deletes the record’s bytes (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentStore"},{"type":"text","text":": once its whole segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is delivered). So a record recovered after a relaunch carries the session it was tracked in,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a destination sends it under the same identifier as before. It is the only part of a record’s context a store keeps, and a store never keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it apart from a record."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/15Instrumentation0A10ContextKeyP","doc:\/\/Events\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Events\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/events\/sessionkey"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" key of the session an event was tracked in: a random identifier that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions(timeout:kinds:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":